    thread_8_summary:Thread 8 = OPEN_POSITIVE_TARGETS.md §P2 — prime gap function pi_h(x) = #{p <= x : p+h prime} batched on h. Closed PARTIAL_POSITIVE_CONDITIONAL at S421 (all 4 slots done). Slot 1 (S418) established EXACT/APPROX dichotomy (EXACT regime Theta(x/log x) per-h P1-shape; APPROX regime HL_h = S_h*li_2(x) polylog per-h with mean|err|/sqrt(x) <= 0.10 P3-shape). Slot 2 (S419) identified cross-h ensemble at fixed x as natural sampling for HL residual analysis (90/90 cells half-Gaussian KS p > 0.1, sigma_eff/sigma_pred_pois in [0.36, 0.70] across (anchor, h) cells, NOT decade-stable). Slot 3 (S420) characterised Q-truncation tradeoff: named-exponent variance decomposition sigma^2_HL_Q = sigma^2_inf + (1/N) sum_{h: max_p_h > Q} (eps_Q li_2)^2 verified at 16 cells across two decades; knee scaling Q* ~ sqrt(x)/log(x) (199 at 10^7, 599-1009 at 10^8); sharp half-Gaussian shape transition Q=100 -> Q=200 (median KS p 0.0015 -> 0.96). Slot 4 (S421, FINAL) lifted the empirical decomposition to a CONDITIONAL THEOREM under the cross-h Hardy-Littlewood Random-Residual Hypothesis (HLRH = three statements: (a) first-moment vanishing, (b) second-moment ~ F^2_H * Sbar_H * li_2(x), (c) cross-h decoherence). Theorem A' (T-A'): (1/N) sum_h (pi_h(x) - S_Q(h)*li_2(x))^2 = (1+o(1)) * F^2_H * Sbar_H * li_2(x) + (1/N) sum_{h:max_p_h>Q} eps_Q(h)^2 * li_2(x)^2 + o(Sbar_H * li_2(x)) for any Q in N union {inf}. Knee Corollary: Q* = sqrt(C(H) * li_2(x) / (F^2_H * Sbar_H)) ~ sqrt(x)/log(x). Corollary B' (algorithmic): polylog-time HL_inf evaluator for h-batches with max h <= (log x)^beta, |H| <= poly(log x), cross-h L^2-typical error eps_typ <= (1+o(1)) F_H * sqrt(Sbar_H * li_2(x)) ~ F_H * sqrt(Sbar_H * x) / log x. 4b extension at x = 10^9 (slot4_x9_extension.py, 66.7s wall): predicted Q* = 1525, empirical knee_max_p in {599, 1009, 2003} — three-decade scaling validation confirmed. Aggregate Thread 8 contribution: polylog-time HL evaluator for h-batches, named-exponent cross-h L^2-typical error, conditional on HLRH; structurally parallel to Thread 7 / S244 K-axis wrap with two structural weakenings (F_H ensemble-dependent, HLRH less-studied than RH+Montgomery). Cross-domain ingredient: Goldston-Montgomery 1987 bilinear-form transposed K-axis -> h-axis (USED-T already, second axis). Project's second A-shape positive-direction CONDITIONAL theorem on adjacent pi-related computation (after Thread 7), first on h-axis.
