    1	# Session 87 — Frontier Attack §D6: Gowers U^k Norms of chi_P
    2	
    3	**Date:** 2026-04-26
    4	**Mode:** Frontier attack (production)
    5	**Target:** ATTACK_VECTORS.md §D6 — Gowers uniformity norms of the bare prime indicator
    6	**Mathematician channel:** Tao (additive combinatorics, mixing arguments, Mobius nilsequence orthogonality)
    7	**Cross-domain technique:** Gowers norms / Green-Tao-Ziegler U^{s+1} inverse theorem (additive combinatorics)
    8	**Self-grade:** **B**
    9	
    10	---
    11	
    12	## Frame
    13	
    14	§D6 was the highest-leverage A-grade target on NOVELTY_CHALLENGES.md
    15	post-S85. The project's pseudorandomness battery has 35+ measures, all
    16	of them either local correlation statistics (autocorrelation, frequency
    17	counts, etc.) or spectral / Boolean / circuit / tensor measures. None
    18	are higher-order *additive-combinatorial* measures — chi_P had never
    19	been tested under any Gowers norm.
    20	
    21	The clean question: does `Q^k(chi_P) := ||chi_P||_{U^k}^{2^k} / E[chi_P]^{2^k}`
    22	converge to a non-trivial limit, and if so, does that limit match the
    23	Hardy-Littlewood {0,1}^k-cube singular series prediction
    24	`S_k = prod_p alpha_p(k) / (1 - 1/p)^{2^k}`?
    25	
    26	A-grade outcome would have been: a deviation from S_k. B-grade was
    27	hypothesis (b) — empirical match to the singular series, providing
    28	a 36th pseudorandomness measure with closed-form prediction.
