    5469	### D41 — Gurau-Witten melonic universality of large-N tensor models on the χ_P 3-tensor
    5470	
    5471	**Question:** Random tensor models (Gurau 2011 *Comm. Math. Phys.*
    5472	304, 69) admit a `1/N` topological expansion *dominated by melonic
    5473	graphs* — fundamentally different from the planar expansion of
    5474	`'t Hooft 1974` for GUE matrices. The melonic large-N limit produces
    5475	*non-Gaussian* universal distributions: the Gurau-Witten / SYK class
    5476	with conformal IR fixed point and non-Wigner density of states (Witten
    5477	2016 arXiv:1610.09758 proved SYK behavior emerges from tensor models
    5478	*without* quenched disorder). Question: define the prime ternary
    5479	3-tensor `T_{ijk}^N := \mathbf{1}[i + j + k = N] \cdot χ_P(i)
    5480	χ_P(j) χ_P(k)` (the Hardy-Littlewood ternary indicator). Compute its
    5481	empirical singular-value distribution under mode-1 unfolding and test
    5482	whether it lies in the **melonic universality class** (non-semicircle,
    5483	heavy-tailed) or in the matrix-rank-2 class (Marchenko-Pastur or
    5484	GUE Wigner semicircle). A non-matrix limit would constitute a NEW
    5485	universality class for χ_P orthogonal to all CLOSED rank-2 measurements
    5486	(C2 sine-kernel, C7 FHK, S74 free cumulants, D31 AHK Chow).
    5487	
    5488	**Why frontier:** every project pseudorandomness measurement on χ_P
    5489	(35+) has tested *rank-2* matrix structure. The Hardy-Littlewood
    5490	*ternary* problem (Vinogradov 1937) is intrinsically rank-3: the
    5491	singular series for `R_3(N) = #\{(p, q, r) : p + q + r = N\}` lives
    5492	on a 3-tensor. **No project measurement has tested rank-3
    5493	universality.** Gurau melonic is the unique known non-Gaussian
    5494	universality class for rank-3 tensors. The χ_P 3-tensor is a natural
    5495	candidate: if it lies in melonic class, this gives the FIRST genuinely
    5496	non-matrix universality result for the prime indicator. Distinct from
    5497	C6 Pfaffian PROPOSED (rank-2 matrix-valued) and from D40 Schur process
    5498	PROPOSED (2D space-time DPP, still rank-2).
